  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The type of the complex&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>MA</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;exhibit the geometrical isomerism fac-mer isomerism.&nbsp;When three ligands and the metal are in one plane, the isomer is said to be meridional, or mer.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></math> can show facial and meridional isomerism.</p>",
